+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
+<!-- osm-urban-us.typ.xml — netconvert type overrides for US URBAN imports.
+     See ADR-0022 (docs/kb/decisions/ADR-0022-us-urban-speed-typemap.md).
+
+     netconvert's built-in OSM typemap is German-derived: highway.secondary,
+     primary and trunk all default to 27.78 m/s (100 km/h). Only 19% of
+     chi-loop's secondary ways carry a maxspeed tag, so 12,945 of its 15,975
+     secondary lanes compiled at 62 mph — Michigan Avenue, Wells, Wabash and
+     State Street all simulated as autobahn. Measured across the tree, 25 US
+     networks were affected; worst was houston-lean at 51.8% of lanes sitting
+     at exactly 100 km/h.
+
+     The unposted defaults here are the STATUTORY urban-district limit —
+     30 mph in Illinois, Texas, Georgia and Florida — not fitted values.
+     Known approximation: California's business/residence default is 25 mph
+     (CVC 22352), so SF/LA imports run 5 mph fast on unposted streets. Fork
+     a per-state map if that ever needs to be exact.
+
+     ONLY the speed attribute differs from the stock typemap: numLanes,
+     priority, oneway, width, allow/disallow and discard are copied
+     verbatim, and no type id is added or dropped. That keeps the diff
+     auditable — it does NOT mean the import is speed-only. netconvert
+     derives right-of-way and signal timing FROM speed:
+
+       * This file MUST be paired with netconvert's
+         "junctions.right-before-left.speed-threshold" option set to 0.
+         (Spelled without its leading dashes here because an XML comment
+         may not contain a double hyphen.) 30 mph = 13.41 m/s is 0.2 m/s
+         below netconvert's default rbl threshold of 13.6111, so without
+         that flag 1,218 chi-loop junctions silently retype from priority
+         to yield-to-the-right. import-city.sh passes both together; do
+         not use this file without it.
+       * Signal phase durations shift (1,936 of chi-loop's 2,217 programs).
+         Yellow tracks approach speed — 3 s at 30 mph instead of 6 s at
+         100 km/h — which is correct, but it means A/B recordings are not
+         comparable at signal-timing level.
+
+     Lane-level topology IS preserved: the chi-loop A/B has identical
+     external lane id sets, origins, exits and signal-program counts.
+     An OSM maxspeed tag still wins over the default.
+
+     NOT for non-US imports — de-roundabouts is German and wants the stock
+     map. Region is a parameter here, not a default.
+
+     Generated from the stock osmNetconvert.typ.xml — regenerate rather
+     than hand-edit if SUMO's typemap changes.
+-->
